✅ Summary of Changes

I’ve adjusted the boilerplate exactly as you asked:

Left‑side admin menu now shows
Expositions, Pieces, Slideshows, Visits, Statistics, Admin
instead of the old entries.
The “Things” functionality is preserved but repurposed:
clicking Expositions opens a familiar list‑and‑create UI backed by the new
Exposition model.
Selecting an exposition displays its pieces and includes a button to add more.
A Pieces page lists all pieces; a Slideshows page lists all slides.
Visits and Statistics are simple placeholder templates.
Admin menu entry redirects to the Django admin (/admin/).
🧩 Under the hood:

New views/URL patterns for expositions, pieces, slides, visits, statistics and
an admin redirect were added to models_views.py and
urls.py.
Templates for the new pages were created in
main_app/templates/main_app/models/….
Action‑column templates (expositions_table_link.html, etc.) direct the user
to show/edit pages.
models.py’s ContentPage now has a ForeignKey to main_app.Piece
so a piece may own multiple Wagtail pages.
A migration (0002_add_piece_to_contentpage.py) adds that field.
Existing “things” code remains untouched (and hidden from the menu) so
nothing breaks if URLs are accessed directly.
